    summary: "The Division of Pediatric Hematology/Oncology at UPMC Children's Hospital of Pittsburgh describes itself as the largest childhood cancer and blood disease centre in western Pennsylvania, eastern Ohio and northern West Virginia, treating all forms of cancer and blood disease in children and adolescents. As a full member of the Children's Oncology Group it says it offers access to nearly 100 active clinical trials. Its programmes include adolescent and young adult oncology, Ewing sarcoma, leukaemia, a melanoma centre, MIBG therapy, neuro-oncology, a paediatric cancer predisposition programme and surgical oncology.",
