    tldr: "The children's cancer and blood disorder programme of Children's Nebraska in Omaha; a Children's Oncology Group member.",
    summary: "The Hematology and Oncology Program at Children's Nebraska diagnoses, treats and follows up children with cancers and blood disorders. Its page says the programme is led by the state's only paediatric haematologists and paediatric oncologists, and that treatment includes chemotherapy and infusion therapies given at a Pediatric Infusion Center open seven days a week. The Children's Survivorship Clinic follows survivors of childhood cancer and bone marrow transplant. The hospital is a member of the Children's Oncology Group, and its physicians take part in COG research and treatment protocols.",
