    tldr: "The children's cancer and blood disorder centre of Connecticut Children's in Hartford; a Children's Oncology Group member.",
    summary: "The Center for Cancer and Blood Disorders at Connecticut Children's cares for children with everything from common blood disorders to the rarest childhood cancers. Treatment plans may include chemotherapy, immunotherapy, surgery, radiation therapy and clinical trials, with support from nutrition, psychology, child life, rehabilitation and social work. Its page says that, as one of more than 200 members of the Children's Oncology Group, it has more than 100 active clinical trials open at any time, and that its researchers are working on treatment plans based on whole-genome analysis of tumours.",
    programs: ["Paediatric haematology and oncology", "Clinical trials (more than 100 open)", "Whole-genome tumour analysis research", "Psychosocial and child life support"],
