    summary: "Dell Children's Blood and Cancer Center provides paediatric cancer and haematology care at Dell Children's sites across Central Texas. Its page says the team performed Central Texas' first successful paediatric autologous bone marrow transplant. Treatment plans may combine chemotherapy, radiation therapy, surgery and bone marrow transplant, and every family is given a nurse navigator who tries to schedule specialist appointments on the same day. Its programmes include bone marrow transplantation, neuro-oncology, cancer predisposition, cardio-oncology, survivorship and leukaemia-lymphoma. It is a member institution of the Children's Oncology Group.",
