    summary: "The Division of Pediatric Hematology-Oncology of the Montreal Children's Hospital cares for children and adolescents with cancer or non-cancerous blood diseases through an inpatient unit with 12 private rooms and a Day Treatment Centre with an oncology satellite pharmacy. Its team includes doctors, nurses, social workers, child life specialists, psychologists, pharmacists, a nutritionist, teachers and art and music therapists. The division's research runs from clinical drug trials to epidemiology and quality-of-life studies. Its page says it is a member of the Children's Oncology Group, the National Wilms Tumor Study Group and the Intergroup Rhabdomyosarcoma Study Group.",
