    summary: "The Cancer and Blood Disorder Center at Driscoll Children's Hospital in Corpus Christi describes itself as the first paediatric cancer centre in South Texas. The hospital says it has taken part in childhood cancer clinical research for more than three decades, and that the centre is a member of the Children's Oncology Group and the National Cancer Institute Community Oncology Research Program (NCORP), giving patients access to more than 100 clinical trials. It reports recognition from the Children's Oncology Group for the highest NCORP enrolment in treatment studies and cancer care delivery research.",
