    summary: "The Inova Children's Cancer Program treats children with cancer at Inova Children's Hospital in Northern Virginia, working with Inova Schar Cancer Institute. Its 22-bed paediatric haematology/oncology unit is a positive-pressure protective-care environment for children with suppressed immune systems. The programme's haematology/oncology physicians, part of Pediatric Specialists of Virginia, are credentialed at both Inova Children's Hospital and Children's National in Washington, DC. Its page says its clinical trial programme is the only Children's Oncology Group member location in Northern Virginia.",
    programs: ["22-bed paediatric haematology/oncology unit", "Clinical trials through the Children's Oncology Group", "Child Life support"],
